<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa April producer price index up 8.8 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>S.Africa April producer price index up 8.8 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 0.4 percent in April from March after rising 0.1 percent in March, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in April was 8.8 percent after March's 9.6 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 0.9 percent month-on-month and 9.5 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Apr'97   Mar'97   Apr'96    - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    8.8	 9.6     5.3	    0.4	0.1</p>
<p>Locally produced   9.7	 9.5     5.9	    1.2	0.2</p>
<p>Imported	     5.4	10.1     3.2	   -3.2     -0.6</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Apr'97    Mar'97    Apr'96</p>
<p>All commodities    113.3     112.9     104.1</p>
<p>Locally produced   114.9     113.5     104.7</p>
<p>Imported	     107.6     111.1     102.1</p>
